DESCRIPTION >
    Super-admin preview: top 5 sources by revenue, trailing 30d. Tenant-scoped;
    prunes via (site_id, timestamp). Faithful 1:1 port of
    api/routes/admin.js:327-339 (queryName 'admin_preview_sources'). Checked
    against all shipped integ_* shapes (suspected match per dispatch note) —
    DIFFERENT: no shipped pipe groups by utm_source with a revenue HAVING
    filter; not a duplicate. Typed-column translation (SCOPE_v3.md §2.6):
    properties.site_id -> site_id, event -> event_type,
    properties.utm_source -> utm_source (typed, Nullable->'direct' on read
    per §2.6 — the live COALESCE(...,'direct') IS the documented read-side
    default, kept verbatim), properties.conversion_value -> conversion_value
    (typed Float64 DEFAULT 0, NOT Nullable).
    REAL TRANSLATION ISSUE, caught by parity validation (not a blind copy):
    the live query wraps in `toFloatOrZero(toString(...))` — `toFloatOrZero`
    is PostHog HogQL sugar, not a native ClickHouse function; running it
    verbatim against Tinybird's own ClickHouse (`tb --cloud sql`) fails with
    "Unknown function toFloatOrZero". Translated to the equivalent native
    function `toFloat64OrZero`, keeping the `toString(...)` wrap (redundant
    against the already-Float64 column but harmless) since only the function
    name is invalid, not the expression shape. No JSON-bag fields.
    NOT YET PUSHED — validated read-only via `tb --cloud sql` only.

NODE admin_preview_sources_node
SQL >
    %
    SELECT
        COALESCE(utm_source, 'direct') AS source,
        sumIf(toFloat64OrZero(toString(conversion_value)), event_type = '$conversion') AS revenue,
        countIf(event_type = '$conversion' AND lower(coalesce(conversion_type, '')) != 'refund') AS conversions
    FROM events
    WHERE site_id = {{ String(site_id, required=True) }}
      AND timestamp >= now() - INTERVAL 30 DAY
    GROUP BY source
    HAVING revenue > 0
    ORDER BY revenue DESC
    LIMIT 5

TYPE endpoint
